1	/**
2	 * Page-level render-test harness — the first in this repository.
3	 *
4	 * Importing this module registers the environment repairs every page-level
5	 * render test needs and that no global vitest config provides (see
6	 * CONTEXT.md):
7	 *
8	 * - an explicit `afterEach(cleanup)` — there is no `globals: true` /
9	 *   `setupFiles`, so Testing-Library's auto-cleanup never registers;
10	 * - a hand-built `localStorage` on `globalThis` — jsdom under vitest 4 in
11	 *   this repo leaves it undefined (Node's own experimental global
12	 *   conflicts), so tests stub a Storage-shaped fake instead;
13	 * - a stubbed `Audio` constructor that records constructed URLs (jsdom's
14	 *   `HTMLMediaElement.play` throws synchronously) plus prototype stubs for
15	 *   `play`/`pause` for any real media element;
16	 * - a stubbed `HTMLCanvasElement.getContext` returning a shared recording
17	 *   2D context (jsdom has none without the `canvas` package), which also
18	 *   lets tests observe `clearRect` calls;
19	 * - `URL.createObjectURL`/`revokeObjectURL` (jsdom implements neither), so
20	 *   any code that turns a `Blob` into a playable URL runs instead of
21	 *   throwing;
22	 * - a `MediaRecorder` recording one fixed `Blob` and a
23	 *   `navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia` whose outcome `setMicPermission`
24	 *   chooses (jsdom has neither) — between them enough for a test to drive
25	 *   `useMicRecorder`'s real state machine, refusal included.
26	 * - a stubbed `fetch` (jsdom has none), returning JSON bodies registered
27	 *   with `stubDeckJson`/`stubDeckFetchError` and 404-ing anything else, for
28	 *   `DeckSlide`'s deck-JSON load.
29	 *
30	 * Test files still need their own `// @vitest-environment jsdom` docblock —
31	 * the pragma only works in the test file itself.
32	 */
